; Sprites: unused page, all zero
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B300+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. This page holds only zero bytes and no entity definition uses it.
@label=UnusedSpritesB3
b$B300 DEFB $00,$00 ; frame 0: blank
